            f"**{int(highlights['coalescing_drift_workers_1_transition_count'])}**",
            "times, with",
            f"**{int(highlights['coalescing_drift_workers_1_transition_causes']['maximum_regret'])}**",
            "changes decided by worst-case regret and none by lexical",
            "tie-breaking.",
            "- Realized Bernoulli paths qualified that dominance. E79",
            "observed no certification regressions across",
            f"**{int(highlights['stochastic_coalescing_cert_comparison_count']):,}**",
            "comparisons, but drift was slower in",
            f"**{fmt(highlights['stochastic_coalescing_drift_regression_fraction'] * 100, 4)}%**",
            "while faster in",
            f"**{fmt(highlights['stochastic_coalescing_drift_faster_fraction'] * 100, 2)}%**.",
            "All eventual actions were retained. False-alarm drift was",
            "the most reversal-sensitive at",
            f"**{fmt(highlights['stochastic_coalescing_drift_false_alarm_rate_regression_fraction'] * 100, 4)}%**",
            "regression.",
            "- Retaining more pending looks reduced average drift risk but",
            "did not create a robust tail guarantee. Depth 16 was the",
            "smallest tested policy below 0.01% aggregate regression,",
            "processing",
            f"**{fmt(highlights['coalescing_depth_drift_16_processed_fraction'] * 100, 2)}%**",
