            f"but reached **{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_bias1_dispatch_speedup'], 3)}x** "
            f"under moderate skew and **{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_bias4_dispatch_speedup'], 3)}x** "
            f"under extreme skew; output cosine stayed above "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_min_output_cosine'], 6)}**.",
            f"- Fusing INT8 reduction/quantization/metadata packing and "
            f"dequantization/unpacking in Triton made 24-GPU balanced dispatch "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_fused_balanced_dispatch_speedup'], 3)}x** "
            f"faster than BF16, though the balanced full layer remained "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_fused_balanced_e2e_speedup'], 3)}x**. "
            f"Moderate and extreme skew reached "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_fused_bias1_e2e_speedup'], 3)}x** and "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_fused_bias4_e2e_speedup'], 3)}x** "
            f"end-to-end.",
            f"- Compressing the expert-output return path added a second small "
            f"collective. At 24 GPUs it raised balanced full-layer speed to "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_roundtrip_balanced_speedup'], 3)}x**, "
            f"was worse than forward-only compression at moderate skew "
            f"(**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_roundtrip_bias1_vs_forward'], 3)}x**), "
            f"and improved extreme-skew performance to "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_roundtrip_bias4_speedup'], 3)}x** "
            f"(**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_roundtrip_bias4_vs_forward'], 3)}x** "
            f"over forward-only).",
            f"- Naively byte-packing the return scale into a 1026-byte row was "
            f"slower than two collectives under all 24-GPU routes. Padding to "
            f"1040 bytes restored alignment and made return communication "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_aligned_balanced_return_vs_two'], 3)}x**, "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_aligned_bias1_return_vs_two'], 3)}x**, and "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_aligned_bias4_return_vs_two'], 3)}x** "
            f"faster than the two-collective path for balanced, moderate, and "
            f"extreme skew.",
            f"- A paired 510/512, 1022/1024, and 4094/4096 width sweep found "
            f"that **{highlights['moe_int8_alignment_smallest_robust_24']}-byte** "
            f"rounding was the smallest 24-GPU packet alignment that beat two "
            f"collectives in every standard-width route: median "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_alignment_24_align16_median'], 3)}x**, "
            f"worst case **{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_alignment_24_align16_min'], 3)}x**. "
            f"The same alignment was not robust intra-node "
            f"(**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_alignment_8_align16_min'], 3)}x** "
            f"worst case).",
            f"- Integrating the aligned packet into the fixed-work three-stage "
            f"pipeline reached **{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_overlap_24_1024_combined_vs_bf16_seq'], 3)}x** "
            f"and **{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_overlap_24_4096_combined_vs_bf16_seq'], 3)}x** "
            f"versus unpipelined BF16 on 24 GPUs. Packetization added only "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_overlap_24_1024_packet_vs_bf16_pipeline'], 3)}x**/"
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_overlap_24_4096_packet_vs_bf16_pipeline'], 3)}x** "
            f"beyond BF16 pipelining, but was "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_overlap_24_1024_packet_vs_two_pipeline'], 3)}x**/"
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_int8_overlap_24_4096_packet_vs_two_pipeline'], 3)}x** "
            f"faster than two-collective INT8 pipelining.",
            f"- Under router-derived variable splits, compression and overlap "
            f"stopped being additive. On 24 GPUs the packet was only "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_variable_overlap_24_balanced_packet_vs_bf16'], 3)}x**/"
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_variable_overlap_24_bias1_packet_vs_bf16'], 3)}x** "
            f"pipelined BF16 for balanced/bias-1 traffic, reaching parity only "
            f"at the **{fmt(highlights['moe_variable_overlap_24_bias4_imbalance'], 1)}x** "
            f"hotspot (**{fmt(highlights['moe_variable_overlap_24_bias4_packet_vs_bf16'], 3)}x**).",
            f"- Putting router/count preparation inside the timed path made the "
            f"24-GPU BF16 staged pipeline "
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_route_prep_24_balanced_bf16_tax'], 3)}x**/"
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_route_prep_24_bias1_bf16_tax'], 3)}x**/"
            f"**{fmt(highlights['moe_route_prep_24_bias4_bf16_tax'], 3)}x** "
