            "",
            "### Suite 0: PyTorch 2.13 `FlexAttention` Quadruple-Defect Audit, SM80 Query-Group Tile Saturation Roofline, Lock-Free Split-`256` `CSC` Backward, & `FP64` Oracle / Richardson Verification",
            "",
            f"- **PyTorch 2.13 `FlexAttention` Dynamic-Mask Quadruple-Defect Audit:** (1) Uncompiled `create_block_mask(H=64, S=16384)` OOMed attempting to materialize a **`{fmt(nsa_fx['defect1_uncompiled_create_block_mask_hq64_s16k']['requested_gib'], 1)} GiB`** `vmap` `int64` index grid (`oom = {nsa_fx['defect1_uncompiled_create_block_mask_hq64_s16k']['oom_triggered_all_reps']}`); (2) `BlockMask.from_kv_blocks` crashed with `{nsa_fx['defect2_from_kv_blocks_transpose_ordered']['error_excerpt']}` whenever `K_sel < N_blocks` because `_transpose_ordered` passed `col_indices.shape[-1]` (`16`) instead of `N_blocks` (`256`) as `num_cols`; (3) fine-grained `BLOCK_SIZE = 64` (`l' = 64` in DeepSeek NSA) failed TorchInductor lowering (`Q_BLOCK_SIZE=64 and KV_BLOCK_SIZE=64` rejected); and (4) compiled `flex_attention` backward (`enable_gqa=True, H_q=64, H_kv=4, D=128`) triggered sticky **`cudaErrorIllegalAddress`** at `S = 65,536` (`S^2 = 2^32` signed `int32` index overflow, verified in isolated child subprocesses across all 3 repetitions).",
            f"- **SM80 Tensor-Core Query-Group Tile Saturation (`S = {nsa_tl['seqlen']}`, `K_sel = 16, B_k = 64`):** Per-head `Quest` (`M = 1` active row per `m16n8k16` MMA tile) collapsed to **`{fmt(nsa_tl['modes']['quest_per_head_m1_64q']['achieved_sparse_tflops_median'], 2)} sparse TFLOP/s` (`{fmt(nsa_tl['modes']['quest_per_head_m1_64q']['ms_median'], 2)} ms`)**; `G = 16` per-token NSA (`64Q/4KV`, `M = 16`) reached **`{fmt(nsa_tl['modes']['nsa_h16_tok1_64q4kv']['achieved_sparse_tflops_median'], 2)} sparse TFLOP/s` (`{fmt(nsa_tl['modes']['nsa_h16_tok1_64q4kv']['ms_median'], 2)} ms`, `{fmt(nsa_tl['tok1_64q_speedup_over_quest_m1'], 2)}x` over `Quest`)**; **`Subchunk-4 x G = 16`** (`M = 64` rows) hit **`{fmt(nsa_tl['modes']['nsa_h16_sub4_64q4kv']['achieved_sparse_tflops_median'], 2)} sparse TFLOP/s` (`{fmt(nsa_tl['modes']['nsa_h16_sub4_64q4kv']['ms_median'], 2)} ms`, `{fmt(nsa_tl['sub4_64q_speedup_over_quest_m1'], 2)}x` over `Quest`)**; and Stride-`16` **`Subchunk-16 x G = 4`** (`32Q/8KV`, `M = 64`) hit **`{fmt(nsa_tl['modes']['nsa_h4_sub16_stride16_32q8kv']['achieved_sparse_tflops_median'], 2)} sparse TFLOP/s` (`{fmt(nsa_tl['modes']['nsa_h4_sub16_stride16_32q8kv']['ms_median'], 2)} ms`, `{fmt(nsa_tl['sub16_32q_speedup_over_tok1_padded_32q'], 2)}x` over padded `G = 4` `{fmt(nsa_tl['modes']['gqa_h4_tok1_padded_32q8kv']['ms_median'], 2)} ms`)**.",
            f"- **Sink-Heavy `FP32` Atomic Collapse vs 100% Lock-Free Split-`256` `CSC` Backward:** Because attention sinks (`kb = 0..2`) are selected by nearly all `S` queries, query-parallel `FP32` `tl.atomic_add` on `dK/dV` stalled at **`{fmt(nsa_cs['S_16384']['query_parallel_fp32_atomic_ms_median'], 2)} ms`** (`S = 16K`) and **`{fmt(nsa_cs['S_32768']['query_parallel_fp32_atomic_ms_median'], 2)} ms`** (`S = 32K`); unsplit `CSC` dropped to `{fmt(nsa_cs['S_16384']['unsplit_csc_sink_straggler_ms_median'], 2)}` / `{fmt(nsa_cs['S_32768']['unsplit_csc_sink_straggler_ms_median'], 2)} ms` (`1`-CTA sink straggler); and our **100% Lock-Free Compacted Work-Tile Split-`256` `CSC`** (`Part_dK/Part_dV` `tl.store` + sequential register reduction, bypassing both L2 ROP contention and Triton 3.7.1's `num_warps=4` `mma -> tl.atomic_add` warp-layout race) finished in **`{fmt(nsa_cs['S_16384']['compacted_worktile_csc_split256_ms_median'], 2)} ms` (`{fmt(nsa_cs['S_16384']['speedup_compacted_csc_over_atomic'], 1)}x` faster than atomics)** at `16K` and **`{fmt(nsa_cs['S_32768']['compacted_worktile_csc_split256_ms_median'], 2)} ms` (`{fmt(nsa_cs['S_32768']['speedup_compacted_csc_over_atomic'], 1)}x` faster than atomics, `{fmt(nsa_cs['S_32768']['speedup_compacted_csc_over_unsplit_csc'], 2)}x` over unsplit `CSC`, `dk/dv rel_l2 = {fmt(nsa_cs['S_32768']['dk_rel_l2_csc_vs_atomic_max'], 5)} / {fmt(nsa_cs['S_32768']['dv_rel_l2_csc_vs_atomic_max'], 5)}`)** at `32K`. `BF16` vs `FP64` exact oracle parity held within `rel_l2 <= {fmt(max(nsa_or.values()), 4)}` across all 10 `NSA` & `MoBA` outputs/gradients, and `FP64` Richardson central-difference ratios across all 8 non-linear derivatives reached **`min = {fmt(nsa_fd['min_ratio'], 4)}x`** (`dv_win` linear FD exact to `{nsa_fd['nsa_dv_win_linear_fd_abs_err_max']:.2e}`).",
