            f"- **Exact 1-GPU Parity & Coupon-Collector Rank-Union Law (`S = 16,384`):** Across `S / 8 = 2,048` tail-rank queries (`512` `sub4` groups), the union of `top-16` induced blocks covered **`{fmt(nsa_c1['coupon_collector_tail_rank_unique_kv_block_union_fraction'] * 100, 2)}%` of all `256` KV blocks** and **`{fmt(nsa_c1['coupon_collector_tail_rank_kv_ranks_touched_fraction'] * 100, 1)}%` of all `8` KV ranks**, proving why sequence-sharded KV-demand fetching degenerates to full-KV `AllGather` (`10,367 MiB/rank` peak HBM at `S = 131K`). Meanwhile, `1D Ulysses-8` (`CP = 8 > H_kv = 4`) splits each `16`-head GQA group across `2` GPUs, incurring `2x` KV head replication plus a quadratic `O(S^2)` `FP32` Eq. (10) score-consensus `AllReduce` (`256 MiB` at `S = 131K`). Our Group-Preserving **`2D USP-NSA (Ulysses-4 x Causal-Asymmetric-ZigZag-2)`** preserves all `G = 16` query heads locally (`0` KV head replication, `0` score `AllReduce`), sends only causal prefix Quarter `0` (`0 -> 1`) while overlapping Quarter `0` compute behind Quarters `1+2` (`1 -> 0`) P2P transfer, and matches 1-GPU `DeepSeek NSA` to **`out rel_l2 = {fmt(nsa_c1['usp_4x2_out_rel_l2_max'], 6)}` (`0.0` bitwise)** and **`dQ / dK_slc / dK_win rel_l2 = {fmt(nsa_c1['usp_4x2_dq_rel_l2_max'], 5)} / {fmt(nsa_c1['usp_4x2_dk_slc_rel_l2_max'], 5)} / {fmt(nsa_c1['usp_4x2_dk_win_rel_l2_max'], 5)}`**.",
